{"id": "EUVD-2026-97688", "enisaUuid": "b59b0f1b-fe55-3617-8c56-a9fda5d7c13f", "description": "FreeRDP from 2.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains an insecure permission vulnerability in winpr-makecert that creates unencrypted private keys without owner-only file modes. Local users on multi-user Unix hosts can read world-readable key files or open PFX files protected by the hard-coded default password to steal private keys.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:56:58", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-2jfv-j3wx-5cg4", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.0.0-before-3.32.0-insecure-private-key-permissions-in-winpr-makecert"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109244", "GHSA-jww6-v76j-hqqx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a997cfc9-3157-3c9c-a22c-8932472ac760", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "eb199682-981e-3433-bdda-fa023dda38d4", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}